# UI components (not entry/bootstrap files)

## Component shape

- Implement UI as **`React.Component` / `PureComponent` subclasses**, not function components. Reserve function components only for app entry/bootstrap if unavoidable (`main.tsx`, root `createRoot`).
- Export the class from the component folder’s `index.tsx` (named export is fine).

## Folder layout (required)

Each component lives in a **camelCase** folder matching the component name, with:

| File | Purpose |
|------|--------|
| `index.tsx` | Component class and JSX |
| `styles.module.css` | All styling (no inline styles in TSX) |
| `types.ts` | Shared `type` aliases only (no `interface`, no `any`) |
| `utils.ts` | Pure helpers used by this component |
| `const.ts` | Constants for this component |

Example: `src/components/appLayout/index.tsx`, `.../appLayout/styles.module.css`, etc.

## Styling

- **No inline styles** — no `style={{ ... }}` on DOM or components. Use CSS Modules classes (`className={styles.foo}`), composition with Ant Design `className` where supported, and global tokens in CSS when needed (e.g. variables from `:root` or Ant theme CSS variables), not JS style objects.

## Routing

- Internal navigation: `react-router-dom` (`Link`, etc.). Class components that need router data should receive props from a parent route element or a small typed wrapper that uses hooks and passes plain props down — avoid scattering hooks in the class file.
